seo-by-rank-math/rank-math.php\";s:11:\"new_version\";s:9:\"1.0.277.2\";s:3:\"url\";s:47:\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/seo-by-rank-math/\";s:7:\"package\";s:69:\"https://downloads.wordpress.org/plugin/seo-by-rank-math.1.0.277.2.zip\";s:5:\"icons\";a:2:{s:2:\"1x\";s:61:\"https://ps.w.org/seo-by-rank-math/assets/icon.svg?rev=3438330\";s:3:\"svg\";s:61:\"https://ps.w.org/seo-by-rank-math/assets/icon.svg?rev=3438330\";}s:7:\"banners\";a:2:{s:2:\"2x\";s:72:\"https://ps.w.org/seo-by-rank-math/assets/banner-1544x500.png?rev=2639678\";s:2:\"1x\";s:71:\"https://ps.w.org/seo-by-rank-math/assets/banner-772x250.png?rev=2639678\";}s:11:\"banners_rtl\";a:0:{}s:8:\"requires\";s:3:\"6.7\";}s:35:\"oa-social-login/oa-social-login.php\";O:8:\"stdClass\":10:{s:2:\"id\";s:29:\"w.org/plugins/oa-social-login\";s:4:\"slug\";s:15:\"oa-social-login\";s:6:\"plugin\";s:35:\"oa-social-login/oa-social-login.php\";s:11:\"new_version\";s:6:\"5.10.0\";s:3:\"url\";s:46:\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/oa-social-login/\";s:7:\"package\";s:58:\"https://downloads.wordpress.org/plugin/oa-social-login.zip\";s:5:\"icons\";a:2:{s:2:\"2x\";s:68:\"https://ps.w.org/oa-social-login/assets/icon-256x256.gif?rev=2680668\";s:2:\"1x\";s:68:\"https://ps.w.org/oa-social-login/assets/icon-128x128.gif?rev=2680668\";}s:7:\"banners\";a:1:{s:2:\"1x\";s:70:\"https://ps.w.org/oa-social-login/assets/banner-772x250.png?rev=2507522\";}s:11:\"banners_rtl\";a:0:{}s:8:\"requires\";s:3:\"3.0\";}s:25:\"wpcode-premium/wpcode.php\";O:8:\"stdClass\":18:{s:4:\"name\";s:6:\"WPCode\";s:4:\"slug\";s:14:\"wpcode-premium\";s:11:\"new_version\";s:5:\"2.3.9\";s:7:\"version\";s:5:\"2.3.9\";s:7:\"package\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"download_url\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"last_updated\";s:19:\"2026-08-27 00:00:00\";s:8:\"requires\";s:3:\"5.0\";s:12:\"requires_php\";s:3:\"7.0\";s:6:\"tested\";s:3:\"7.1\";s:11:\"description\";s:547:\"<p>WPCode Pro Allows you to:</p> <ul> <li>Save Code Snippets to Your Private Cloud Library (Save Time)</li> <li>Add Page &amp; Device Specific Snippets Right Inside WordPress Editor</li> <li>Add snippets using advanced eCommerce Locations &amp; Conditional logic rules for WooCommerce and Easy Digital Downloads</li> <li>Save &amp; View advanced Code Revisions in a friendly human-readable way. 1-click restore!</li> <li>Load your favourite snippets from the WPCode Library directly in the WordPress dashboard</li> <li>And many more...</li> </ul> \";s:9:\"changelog\";s:41407:\"<p>= 2.3.9 =</p> <ul> <li>Fix: PHP fatal error when a snippet error was logged on a frontend or REST request while the logs folder was missing.</li> <li>Fix: Snippets no longer get overwritten with visual editor content when other plugins trigger editor events in the admin.</li> <li>Fix: Library snippet previews now always start at the top of the code.</li> <li>Fix: The Page Scripts admin bar link now opens and scrolls to the panel on WordPress 7.1.</li> <li>Fix: The license key is now saved at the network level on multisite.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.3.8 =</p> <ul> <li>Tweak: You can now resize the code editor on the Live CSS Preview screen by dragging the divider between it and the preview, and it remembers the size you set.</li> <li>Tweak: Editing an active snippet now requires permission to activate snippets; without it the editor is read-only.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.3.7 =</p> <ul> <li>New: Set up a whole group of related snippets at once with Snippet Packs. Pick a pack and install every snippet in it with a single click, then manage or remove a pack anytime.</li> <li>Fix: Snippets that use the \"Load as File\" option now keep their code exactly as written.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.3.6 =</p> <ul> <li>New: You can now easily tell where each library snippet came from — imported snippets show a small cloud badge and the originating library author (WPCode, WPForms, AIOSEO, and more).</li> <li>Tweak: We improved how the snippet library handles unexpected cache or server errors, so the library tab keeps working reliably and failed imports no longer leave behind blank snippets.</li> <li>Tweak: We added extra permission checks around snippet creation and editing to ensure only authorized users can make changes.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.3.5 =</p> <ul> <li>New: Visual CSS selector picker for \"Insert Anywhere\" locations: pick elements directly from your page.</li> <li>Fix: \"Load as file\" option not showing for new unsaved CSS/JS/SCSS snippets.</li> <li>Fix: Switching a snippet from shortcode back to auto-insert mode now correctly restores the selected location.</li> <li>Fix: Changes made in the Text tab of the visual editor for text snippets are now saved correctly.</li> <li>Fix: Resolved a fatal error that could occur when the snippet library cache returns invalid data.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.3.4 =</p> <ul> <li>New: Integration with the WordPress Abilities API (requires WordPress 6.9+).</li> </ul> <p>= 2.3.3 =</p> <ul> <li>New: You can now choose to load PHP, HTML and Universal snippets from files instead of the database. This may improve performance and enables external version control for your snippets.</li> <li>Tweak: Improved compatibility with PHP 8.5.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.3.2.1 =</p> <ul> <li>Fix: Fixed an issue where users who can\'t edit snippets saw an error message.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.3.2 =</p> <ul> <li>New: You can now see style changes you make in real time with our Live Preview feature for CSS &amp; SCSS snippets.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.3.1 =</p> <ul> <li>New: The Conversion Pixels addon can now use multiple pixels for Facebook and Google tracking.</li> <li>New: We added a 1-click license refresh button to the settings page.</li> <li>Fix: We changed the way labels are loaded in conditional logic classes to avoid notices when used with \"Run Everywhere\" snippets.</li> <li>Fix: We fixed an issue with notices being thrown in certain setups when saving advanced settings.</li> <li>Tweak: Smart Tags are now available in more fields for generators.</li> <li>Tweak: Force refresh editor in the snippet generator to display gutters correctly.</li> <li>Tweak: Added extra checks for the WPCode settings option to ensure it\'s always the correct format and avoid notices in edge cases when the option is cleared externally.</li> <li>Tweak: Minimum PHP version updated to 7.0.</li> <li>Tweak: Minimum WP version updated to 5.0.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.3.0 =</p> <ul> <li>New: We added a way to 1-click update snippets installed from the WPCode library when new versions are available. This includes snippets in your private library for which you will immediately see which snippets have updates available in the admin of your connected sites.</li> <li>Tweak: We improved JSON code snippets import validation to show accurate error messages when files are incorrectly formatted.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.2.9 =</p> <ul> <li>New: We added 38 new smart tags to enhance the way you write snippets with less code. These include more tags for plugins like WooCommerce, Easy Digital Downloads, MemberPress, All in One SEO and Yoast SEO.</li> <li>New: We added a new importer for the Post Snippets plugin to make switching to WPCode easier.</li> <li>Tweak: We adjusted the way the safe mode works to limit its effects on frontend urls.</li> <li>Fix: We fixed a bug where restoring a revision would remove backslashes from code.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.2.8 =</p> <ul> <li>New: Schema Generators - we added 20 new code generators to make it easier to manage schema code on your website.</li> <li>Tweak: We moved the button to update generated snippets to the top so that you can update snippets easier.</li> <li>Tweak: We added \"suppress_filters\" to WP_Query used by WPCode to avoid conflicts with other plugins.</li> <li>Fix: We fixed an issue where the generated snippets were not automatically inserted when activated.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.2.7 =</p> <ul> <li>New: You can now compress the output for HTML, JS and CSS snippets. This removes comments and spaces making your snippet output smaller.</li> <li>New: Automatically import snippets from 2 new plugins.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.2.6 =</p> <ul> <li>New: Easily find where your snippet is used as a shortcode with our new shortcode finder tool. 1-click search through your site.</li> <li>New: Improved editor for snippet notes. You can now add links and format text with a WYSIWYG editor.</li> <li>New: Snippet notes column. Display the notes for each snippet in the list of snippets.</li> <li>Tweak: Improved search for WooCommerce cart conditional logic with support for SKU and product variations.</li> <li>Fix: We improved the code snippets list filtering in the admin to avoid issues when JS errors are encountered on the page from other scripts.</li> <li>Fix: We fixed an issue with code slashing when pushing updates from the library in certain scenarios.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.2.5 =</p> <ul> <li>New: We added a new way to quickly filter snippets by code type in the list of snippets.</li> <li>Tweak: Prevent content_save_pre from modifying snippet code.</li> <li>Tweak: Code types you can\'t edit are no longer displayed when editing a snippet.</li> <li>Fix: We fixed an issue with snippets inserted every n words.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.2.4.1 =</p> <ul> <li>Fix: Shortcode attributes variables were not being set correctly.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.2.4 =</p> <ul> <li>New: We added Post Meta and User Meta conditional logic rules for even more control on where your snippets are loaded.</li> <li>Tweak: We adjusted the way we add a version-specific body class to avoid conflicts with other plugins.</li> <li>Tweak: We improved the way custom PHP code is executed to avoid conflicts with variables in snippets.</li> <li>Fix: When removing the last Conditional Logic group the rule selector was no longer working.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.2.3.1 =</p> <ul> <li>Tweak: We updated the way we load translatable strings in some components for compatibility with WordPress 6.7.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.2.3 =</p> <ul> <li>New: SCSS code type, you can now write SCSS code directly in WPCode and it will get automatically compiled to CSS that can be inserted inline or loaded as a file in the frontend.</li> <li>Tweak: We updated the way we check PHP snippet edits for active snippets for more feedback when making edits to a snippet.</li> <li>Tweak: We replaced a dependency (SweetAlert2) for a more lightweight alternative to improve performance.</li> <li>Tweak: We updated the label for the EDD Success page to match the current Confirmation page for more clarity in conditional logic options.</li> <li>Tweak: We increased the timeout when saving snippets to the WPCode library for improved compatibility with different hosting environments.</li> <li>Fix: The code picker is now automatically hidden when creating a new snippet with AI.</li> <li>Fix: Deleting snippets from the \"My Library\" area was not working correctly.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.2.2.1 =</p> <ul> <li>Fix: Blocks snippet auto embed callback was incorrect.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.2.2 =</p> <ul> <li>New: The Add Snippet screen now makes it easier to get started with more than just our library of snippets, choose from expert-picked snippets, snippet generators or plugin-specific snippets.</li> <li>New: We updated the code type picker for more clarity on what each code type is useful for and the last code type you used is now saved for a streamlined experience when adding multiple snippets.</li> <li>Tweak: We extended the unfiltered HTML permissions notice when the DISALLOW_UNFILTERED_HTML constant is defined to add more clarity.</li> <li>Fix: We fixed a notice that was being thrown in PHP 8.2 when our Insert Anywhere locations are used.</li> <li>Fix: Using embed blocks in the Blocks code type snippets was not always working correctly.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.2.1 =</p> <ul> <li>New: Conditional Logic rules for authors, show snippets only on posts by certain authors.</li> <li>New: Conditional Logic rules for Page Templates, load snippets only on specific page templates from your theme.</li> <li>New: Dynamic content insert locations, automatically place a snippet in the middle of an article or other common locations: 1st 3rd, 2nd 3rd, 1st quarter, 3rd quarter, etc.</li> <li>Fix: We fixed a bug that was causing the selected conditional logic operator to not be displayed correctly for some rules.</li> <li>Fix: The auto-insert location picker was not opening again in some situations.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.2.0 =</p> <ul> <li>New: You can now push snippet updates from the library to your website without logging in. You need to reconnect to the WPCode library from the WPCode Settings to opt-in to this feature.</li> <li>New: We updated the conditional logic rules picker for more clarity and ease of use.</li> <li>New: We expanded our automatic cache clearing to include the Swift Performance plugin.</li> <li>Tweak: The Page URL conditional logic option now supports query params and wp-admin URLs.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.1.14 =</p> <ul> <li>New: WPCode AI Integration: You can now generate new snippets or enhance existing PHP snippets using natural language directly in the WordPress admin with the new WPCode AI integration. This feature is available to all users on Pro and higher plans.</li> <li>New: When making changes to the Global Header &amp; Footer WPCode will attempt to automatically clear page cache for popular caching plugins.</li> <li>New: Save your snippet with a keyboard shortcut by pressing CTRL+S (Windows) or CMD+S (Mac) in the snippet editor.</li> <li>Tweak: Improve the order of results when searching for posts in the Post/Page conditional logic conditions.</li> <li>Tweak: Prevent error when TinyMCE is disabled by other plugins.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.1.13 =</p> <ul> <li>New: A new addon for Location-based Conditional Logic rules is now available to all our Pro users. Limit where your snippets are loaded based on the user\'s Country or Continent.</li> <li class=\"li1\">New: We added admin-specific locations for header and footer to streamline customizations in the wp-admin area.</li> <li class=\"li1\">New: The code editor height can now be adjusted directly from the snippet editor screen. Auto-height is still available as an option on the settings page.</li> <li class=\"li1\">Fix: We changed the way updates are handled in multisite environments to allow updating the core plugin with non-elite plans.</li> <li class=\"li1\">Fix: When making changes to a snippet, the function to prevent you from navigating away was no longer working.</li> <li>Fix: There were scenarios where the conditional logic with a negate operator was not working as intended.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.1.12 =</p> <ul> <li>New: We added a new way to execute PHP snippets - look for the \"On Demand\" location in the Auto Insert settings.</li> <li>New: A new Permalink Smart Tag is now available.</li> <li>Tweak: We added checks in place to prevent malicious code patterns from being used in WPCode.</li> <li>Fix: We fixed a bug where the conditional logic for logged-in users was not being saved correctly the first time.</li> <li>Fix: Restoring revisions from the “Compare” view was not working correctly.</li> <li>Fix: The “Disable Global Scripts” option in Page Scripts was not working as intended.</li> <li>Fix: The Page Scripts revisions were not loading correctly in some situations.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.1.11 =</p> <ul> <li>New: You can now choose to load JavaScript or CSS snippets as files through the WP enqueue system for more performance options.</li> <li>Tweak: We improved the admin bar menu to fix an JS error in some scenarios and a html validation issue.</li> <li>Tweak: We added support for importing snippets from the Code Snippets Pro plugin.</li> <li>Fix: We fixed an issue with importing CSS snippets.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.1.10 =</p> <ul> <li>New: Elementor Widget for WPCode snippets - it’s now easier than ever to insert snippets in Elementor with support for shortcode attributes.</li> <li>New: When another user is editing the same snippet, we now show a warning to avoid conflicts.</li> <li class=\"li1\">New: WPCode is now translated in 10 languages: Dutch, French, German, Italian, Japanese, Polish, Portuguese, Russian, Spanish and Turkish.</li> <li class=\"li1\">Tweak: Improved mobile styles across the plugin admin for better readability.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.1.9 =</p> <ul> <li>New: Multisite Addon is now available for Elite plan users - manage snippets and scripts across your multisite network in a familiar interface.</li> <li class=\"li1\">New: Conditional logic rule for Blog home page (posts page)</li> <li>Tweak: Improved the connect to library flow to avoid the connect window from getting blocked.</li> <li class=\"li1\">Tweak: Improved compatibility with the TranslatePress plugin where in some situations it would create an endless loop.</li> <li class=\"li1\">Fix: Author archive condition was not working as intended.</li> <li class=\"li1\">Fix: MemberPress plan conditional logic picker.</li> <li class=\"li1\">Fix: WooCommerce “in cart” conditional logic picker.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.1.8 =</p> <ul> <li class=\"li1\">New: Conditional logic rules based on another WPCode snippet being loaded.</li> <li>New: Conditional logic rules by specific post/page using the post id.</li> <li>New: Conditional logic rules based on Cookies in the visitor browser.</li> <li>New: Conditional logic rules based on the visitor Browser and Operating system.</li> <li>New: Auto-insert locations based on the number of words in an article. Insert snippet after a minimum number of words or once every x number of words without breaking paragraphs.</li> <li>Tweak: We changed the way the code generators are loaded to improve performance overall.</li> <li>Fix: Fixed a conflict with some plugins when using the classic editor.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.1.7 =</p> <ul> <li class=\"li1\">New: Email notifications for snippet errors and snippet deactivations - check out the new Error Handling tab under Settings.</li> <li>New: WPCode now has a Dark Mode for those late night coding sessions. Enable it on the settings page.</li> <li>Tweak: We improved the way the error messages are displayed in the snippet editor for more clarity.</li> <li>Fix: The snippet editor was no longer running syntax checks for PHP snippets upon activation.</li> <li>Fix: We fixed a bug where in certain versions of Safari the auto-insert location was being unset when saving a snippet.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.1.6 =</p> <ul> <li class=\"li1\">New: Advanced code revisions for Global Header &amp; Footer scripts and WPCode Page Scripts are now available. As you make changes to your scripts you’ll be able to restore previous versions with 1 click.</li> <li>New: We added an option in the settings panel to delete all WPCode data when the plugin is uninstalled.</li> <li>Fix: When duplicating a snippet slashes were being removed in certain cases.</li> <li>Fix: The error count was not correctly updated when snippets were trashed.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.1.5.1 =</p> <ul> <li class=\"li1\">Fix: Added extra checks to avoid errors from permission checks in some setups.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.1.5 =</p> <ul> <li class=\"li1\">New: WPCode Testing Mode - make changes that are visible just to you and choose when to publish them to all visitors.</li> <li>New: Priority column added to the list of snippets, order by snippet priority.</li> <li>Fix: Fixed a notice that was being thrown in new sites when running the installation routines.</li> <li>Fix: Filtering by tag or location in the list of snippets was not working correctly.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.1.4.1 =</p> <ul> <li>Fix: Avoid notices for errors that don\'t include the file parameter.</li> <li>Fix: Improve compatibility with PHP 8.2 for the snippet cache class.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.1.4 =</p> <ul> <li>New: Improved error tracking, errors thrown by PHP snippets loaded on your site are now tracked and reported in the snippet context for easier debugging.</li> <li>New: We improved the way snippets get automatically deactivated so that only snippets that throw fatal errors in the admin are deactivated, all other errors will be reported using the new error tracker.</li> <li>New: We added 3 new columns to the list of snippets: id, code type and shortcode.</li> <li>Tweak: We improved the way we handle file caching to avoid repeated requests when files can’t be written correctly in some setups.</li> <li>Tweak: We added an extra check to prevent closing PHP tags from breaking execution of snippets.</li> <li>Fix: We fixed the order of snippets when ordered by the last updated date.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.1.3.1 =</p> <ul> <li>Fix: Shortcode attributes were not being correctly parsed in some scenarios.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.1.3 =</p> <ul> <li>New: You can now add snippets directly in the code editor using the brand new WPCode Snippet Block and configure attributes in an easy to use interface.</li> <li>New: We improved how we manage automatic snippet disabling when errors occur. You\'ll now get detailed insights into which snippet is responsible for the error and the exact line where the problem occurred.</li> <li>Tweak: We adjusted the way snippets are preloaded to improve compatibility with object cache.</li> <li>Fix: We adjusted the way the timestamps for the revisions are saved to display the correct time.</li> <li>Fix: The snippets added as shortcodes were not correctly displayed in the admin bar.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.1.2.1 =</p> <ul> <li>Fix: Save button was not loaded correctly on the settings page.</li> <li>Fix: The WPCode admin bar menu was not showing all the items correctly in the admin area.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.1.2 =</p> <ul> <li>New: Access Control settings now allow you to empower other users to manage snippets based on the code type or update conversion pixels settings and use the file editor.</li> <li>New: Scripts added by the Conversion Pixels addon are now listed in the Admin Bar Code Spotter in the locations where they are placed.</li> <li>Tweak: We adjusted the way snippets are tracked in the Admin Bar Code Spotter to avoid wrong numbers in certain locations.</li> <li>Tweak: We improved the way the Admin Bar Code Spotter menu is loaded for better compatibility with other plugins and older themes.</li> <li>Tweak: We changed the way assets used by the admin bar are loaded to avoid errors if the head is loaded multiple times.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.1.1 =</p> <ul> <li>New: Edit configuration files like ads.txt, app-ads.txt, service-worker.js and robots.txt files directly from the admin with the WPCode File Editor.</li> <li>New: Easily duplicate a snippet with all of its settings with the new Duplicate link in the list of snippets.</li> <li>Fix: Taxonomy page conditional logic was not being correctly assigned for category and tags archives.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.1.0 =</p> <ul> <li>New: See exactly which scripts and snippets are loaded on the current page with the WPCode admin bar info menu.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.0.13.1 =</p> <ul> <li>Fix: Improve compatibility with older WordPress versions before version 4.7.</li> <li>Fix: Add escaping to tag filter links in the list of snippets.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.0.13 =</p> <ul> <li>New: We have added a new auto-insert location that enables you to completely replace an HTML element using a CSS selector with the contents of your snippet, providing even more customization power.</li> <li>New: You can now create conditional logic rules based on the WooCommerce cart contents. Choose one or more products that need to be in the cart for your snippet to take effect.</li> <li>New: We have added user customization options for the list of snippets in the admin. Now, you can choose snippet list columns, determine the number of snippets to display, and set the default order of the snippets.</li> <li>New: When you save a snippet, the WPCode editor will retain the cursor position, making it easier for you to continue editing larger snippets.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.0.12 =</p> <ul> <li>New: You can now use Smart Tags in HTML, Text, JavaScript and Universal snippets enabling you to add variables to your snippets without having to code.</li> <li>New: You can now add Shortcode Attributes and use them in snippets. Any attribute you define becomes available as a variable in PHP code snippets &amp; you can use them as smart tags in other snippet types.</li> <li>New: We added more smart tags for: custom field value, author name, author id, author URL, login URL and logout URL.</li> <li>Tweak: We improved the way the editor is loaded when users enable the “Disable syntax highlighting when editing code” in their profile.</li> <li>Tweak: We updated when the page scripts are loaded so that you can use them to extend global scripts.</li> <li>Tweak: We adjusted the way the editor gets refreshed when changing a snippet code type.</li> <li>Fix: The Auto-Insert location was getting reset with every code type change.</li> <li>Fix: In some instances the page scripts code editor was not refreshed correctly and appeared blank before clicking it.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.0.11 =</p> <ul> <li>New: Brand new MemberPress integration - use Auto-Insert Locations and Conditional Logic rules to extend your MemberPress site easier than ever.</li> <li>New: Snippets that are automatically disabled due to an error are now highlighted in the list of snippets so that you can fix the issues faster.</li> <li>New: We added a filter to allow users to easily customize the CodeMirror settings for the WPCode editor.</li> <li>Tweak: We extended our plugin-specific snippet loading to allow plugin version checks.</li> <li>Tweak: We added an extra check to ensure the block editor is available for the snippet Blocks.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.0.10 =</p> <ul> <li>New: You can now use the Gutenberg Block Editor to create blocks snippets. Choose the Blocks Snippet code type to get started.</li> <li>New: We added a way to load more snippets in the WPCode Library relevant to other plugins you are using.</li> <li>Fix: We added an extra filter removal to prevent WordPress core from automatically adding the rel tag to snippets where it may break the syntax.</li> <li>Fix: The library used for inserting snippets anywhere was being loaded even when not needed so we limited that to improve compatibility.</li> <li>Fix: We improved backwards compatibility with older WordPress &amp; PHP versions.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.0.9 =</p> <ul> <li>New: Insert snippets anywhere using CSS Selectors to target any HTML element on your site regardless of the available hooks.</li> <li class=\"p1\">New: We redesigned the auto-insert location picker to make it easier to find the right place to insert your snippets.</li> <li>Fix: We fixed an edge-case where a snippet getting automatically deactivated due to throwing an error would have its code changed.</li> <li>Fix: Inserting a snippet as a shortcode was ignoring the conditional logic rules enable toggle and always applying rules.</li> <li>Fix: We updated the way we check the taxonomy term id when applying conditional logic rules.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.0.8.1 =</p> <ul> <li>Fix: Improve compatibility with PHP 8.1 for our error handling class.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.0.8 =</p> <ul> <li class=\"li1\">New: We added the option to Schedule snippets with a date interval and also create advanced schedules with conditional logic options.</li> <li class=\"li1\">New: We added the option to log PHP errors thrown by snippets added with WPCode to make it easier to track down issues.</li> <li class=\"li1\">New: We added a new auto-insert location to improve the available conditional logic rules you can use with PHP snippets.</li> <li class=\"li1\">Tweak: We added more info regarding the error thrown when trying to activate a PHP snippet with a syntax error.</li> <li class=\"li1\">Tweak: Conditional logic rules are now also applied to shortcodes for better control of output.</li> <li class=\"li1\">Tweak: The shortcode output now also takes into consideration the device type setting.</li> <li class=\"li1\">Tweak: We updated the code editor for PHP snippets to give you a better experience when editing snippets.</li> <li class=\"li1\">Fix: We adjusted the permission checks of some ajax endpoints to avoid any potential unwanted usage.</li> <li class=\"li1\">Fix: The Safe Mode notice was no longer being displayed on the WPCode pages, so we added that back when needed.</li> <li class=\"li1\">Fix: We improved accessibility for multiple inputs in the WPCode admin area.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.0.7 =</p> <ul> <li>New: The Conversion Pixels addon is here, start tracking Facebook, Google, Pinterest and TikTok pixels with no coding required, available to all our users with a Plus or higher license directly from the WPCode plugin or your account area.</li> <li> <p class=\"p1\">New: We added the ability to resume editing snippets that were created using the WPCode snippet generator.</p> </li> <li> <p class=\"p1\">Fix: We adjusted the code output in the editor to improve support for using HTML entities.</p> </li> <li>Fix: We updated the order of some checks to ensure the WooCommerce thank you page conditional logic works correctly.</li> <li>Fix: We made sure conditional logic rules are loaded correctly in the admin when used globally.</li> <li>Fix: We added an extra permissions check to the library endpoints to limit access.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.0.6 =</p> <ul> <li>New: WPCode Library public snippets can now be installed with 1-click on sites connected to the WPCode Library - no more copy/paste needed!</li> <li>New: We added a setting for the editor height, so you can set the editor to a custom height or make it automatically grow with the code.</li> <li>Tweak: We adjusted the \"Connect To Library\" functionality to improve support for site names with special characters or empty names.</li> <li>Fix: We added extra checks to prevent errors when certain conditional logic rules were being called too early with PHP snippets.</li> <li>Fix: The revisions output would show some notices related to conditional logic changes and we added some extra checks to prevent those.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.0.5 =</p> <ul> <li class=\"li1\">New: Choose which device to load the snippet on with just 1-click with our brand-new device type picker in the snippet editor.</li> <li class=\"li1\">New: Device type (desktop/mobile) is now also available for conditional logic rules for more granular control.</li> <li class=\"li1\">New: 2 new bulk actions are available in the admin to allow enabling or disabling multiple snippets at once.</li> <li class=\"li1\">New: We added a new search field for snippets in the admin list which allows you to search using all snippet fields.</li> <li class=\"li1\">New: When adding a JavaScript snippet, WPCode will attempt to remove HTML script tags, if present.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.0.4.3 =</p> <ul> <li>Tweak: We updated the default behaviour of our page scripts metabox so that it is collapsed by default.</li> <li>Fix: We fixed a bug where our metabox scripts were interfering with other plugins in the classic editor view.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.0.4.2 =</p> <ul> <li>Tweak: Changing SweetAlert library version to prevent the interference on .ru sites.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.0.4.1 =</p> <ul> <li>Fix: Certain checks for our WooCommerce and EDD integrations were triggering errors in the frontend.</li> </ul> <p class=\"p1\">= 2.0.4 =</p> <ul> <li class=\"p1\">New: The first version of the WPCode Pro plugin includes many powerful features listed below.</li> <li class=\"p1\">Private Snippets Library: Save Snippets to your WPCode Library privately directly from the plugin and import them in any other site using WPCode Premium.</li> <li class=\"p1\">Advanced Code Revisions: See a list of all the changes made to your snippet and who made the change so you can easily test new settings and restore old ones.</li> <li class=\"p1\">Page-Specific scripts: Use the WPCode metabox to add custom scripts specific to a page in the Header, Footer or Body, also load any custom snippet in the specific page context by selecting it from a list.</li> <li class=\"p1\">eCommerce Insert Locations: Target specific relevant insert locations for your WooCommerce ore Easy Digital Downloads site by selecting from a list of relevant locations.</li> <li class=\"p1\">eCommerce Conditional Logic: The Smart Conditional Logic fields allow you to create complex rules in an easy-to-use interface using WooCommerce or Easy Digital Downloads conditions.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>New: You can now add snippets directly in the code editor using the brand new WPCode Snippet Block and configure attributes in an easy to use interface.</li> <li>New: We improved how we manage automatic snippet disabling when errors occur. You\'ll now get detailed insights into which snippet is responsible for the error and the exact line where the problem occurred.</li> <li>Tweak: We adjusted the way snippets are preloaded to improve compatibility with object cache.</li> <li>Fix: We adjusted the way the timestamps for the revisions are saved to display the correct time.</li> <li>Fix: The snippets added as shortcodes were not correctly displayed in the admin bar.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.1.2.1 =</p> <ul> <li>Fix: Save button was not loaded correctly on the settings page.</li> <li>Fix: The WPCode admin bar menu was not showing all the items correctly in the admin area.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.1.2 =</p> <ul> <li>New: Access Control settings now allow you to empower other users to manage snippets based on the code type or update conversion pixels settings and use the file editor.</li> <li>New: Scripts added by the Conversion Pixels addon are now listed in the Admin Bar Code Spotter in the locations where they are placed.</li> <li>Tweak: We adjusted the way snippets are tracked in the Admin Bar Code Spotter to avoid wrong numbers in certain locations.</li> <li>Tweak: We improved the way the Admin Bar Code Spotter menu is loaded for better compatibility with other plugins and older themes.</li> <li>Tweak: We changed the way assets used by the admin bar are loaded to avoid errors if the head is loaded multiple times.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.1.1 =</p> <ul> <li>New: Edit configuration files like ads.txt, app-ads.txt, service-worker.js and robots.txt files directly from the admin with the WPCode File Editor.</li> <li>New: Easily duplicate a snippet with all of its settings with the new Duplicate link in the list of snippets.</li> <li>Fix: Taxonomy page conditional logic was not being correctly assigned for category and tags archives.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.1.0 =</p> <ul> <li>New: See exactly which scripts and snippets are loaded on the current page with the WPCode admin bar info menu.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.0.13.1 =</p> <ul> <li>Fix: Improve compatibility with older WordPress versions before version 4.7.</li> <li>Fix: Add escaping to tag filter links in the list of snippets.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.0.13 =</p> <ul> <li>New: We have added a new auto-insert location that enables you to completely replace an HTML element using a CSS selector with the contents of your snippet, providing even more customization power.</li> <li>New: You can now create conditional logic rules based on the WooCommerce cart contents. Choose one or more products that need to be in the cart for your snippet to take effect.</li> <li>New: We have added user customization options for the list of snippets in the admin. Now, you can choose snippet list columns, determine the number of snippets to display, and set the default order of the snippets.</li> <li>New: When you save a snippet, the WPCode editor will retain the cursor position, making it easier for you to continue editing larger snippets.</li> </ul> <p>= 2.0.12 =</p> <ul> <li>New: You can now use Smart Tags in HTML, Text, JavaScript and Universal snippets enabling you to add variables to your snippets without having to code.</li> <li>New: You can now add Shortcode Attributes and use them in snippets. Any attribute you define becomes available as a variable in PHP code snippets &amp; you can use them as smart tags in other snippet types.</li> <li>New: We added more smart tags for: custom field value, author name, author id, author URL, login URL and logout URL.</li